WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.500
Ever since it hit theaters in August 2017,
Annabelle: Creation has scared the pants off

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.300
millions of fans — and finally revealed
just where that demonic doll from The Conjuring

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.300
really came from.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.780
But if this horror origin story left you with
more questions than answers, don't be afraid!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.800
We've got everything you need to know about
the film's ending and post-credits scenes…

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.370
unless you don't want to see spoilers for
The Conjuring and both Annabelle films, in

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.519
which case this is your cue to cover your
eyes and hide under the covers until the video

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:28.570
is over.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.210
The doll is just a vessel

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.880
Annabelle might be inherently creepy, but
before she became infested by an evil spirit,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.940
she was just a very expensive, hand-crafted
doll — and the part where she has a face

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.570
like something out of a nightmare?

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.250
An unfortunate coincidence.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.929
The origin of Annabelle's evil comes when
the Mullins invite the spirit of their deceased

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:49.980
daughter to live inside the doll, only to
realize that the entity in that porcelain

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.809
body isn't a human ghost at all, but something
ancient, powerful, and extraordinarily evil.

00:00:55.809 --> 00:01:00.219
With the help of some Catholic priests, Samuel
Mullins manages to trap the doll in a closet

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:03.180
lined with scripture, and he hopes that'll
be the end of it.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.751
But while scripture might keep the demon in,
it won't keep curious little girls out, which

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.480
brings us to this:

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.980
Annabelle's first jailbreak

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:16.220
To atone for their accidental dealings with
the devil, the Mullins generously invite Sister

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:19.060
Charlotte and her six orphans to come live
with them.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.279
The house rules are simple: do your chores,
be polite, and don't open the evil closet

00:01:23.279 --> 00:01:25.170
— yes, that evil closet.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.170
Stop!

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.290
What are you doing?!

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.290
[Door creaking]

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.680
Horror predictably ensues from here, as the
free-at-last evil spirit proceeds to terrorize

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:37.650
the household, possess Janice, and do away
with both Mr. and Mrs. Mullins.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:41.710
Eventually, Sister Charlotte saves the day
by trapping both the possessed Janice and

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.880
the doll in the scripture closet and calling
the cops — but when they show up, the only

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:50.119
thing in the closet is the doll… and the
hole in the wall where Janice presumably blasted

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.100
through like the Kool-Aid man and made her
escape.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.560
Demon for adoption

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.200
Now occupying the body of an adorable child
and calling itself "Annabelle," the demon

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:04.570
makes its way to an orphanage and is immediately
adopted by the Higgins family — with whom

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.079
it lives happily ever after.

00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:12.610
...Or at least until 1967, when we see a grownup
Annabelle return home and brutalize her parents,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.690
which causes a ruckus that wakes up the neighbors,
who are of course the central characters of

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.470
the first standalone Annabelle movie.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:23.030
Roll credits, and mission accomplished: you've
just watched a terrifying origin story that

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:27.690
enjoys perfect continuity with the rest of
the Conjuring universe.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:28.690
Annabelle explained

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.720
You don't have to have seen the first Annabelle
to enjoy the Creation origin story, but if

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.220
you did, Creation answers some important questions
about the events from that film.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.520
For one, we can safely assume that Annabelle,
who was really a possessed Janice, didn't

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.410
take out her adoptive parents in a cultist
attempt to "resurrect the Ram."

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.640
She is the Ram!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.640
[Screaming]

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:52.180
So when Annabelle-slash-Janice offs her parents,
slits her own throat, and bleeds into the

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:57.000
doll's eyeball, the demon possessing her moves
back into the first vessel it ever occupied

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.620
— and sets its sights on a new human target.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:04.340
The Ram clearly has a thing for kids, which
may explain why it's so drawn to this porcelain

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.480
body; where a creepy doll goes, children are
sure to follow.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.700
The bigger picture

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:13.880
Let's not forget that Annabelle: Creation
is a part of the larger universe of the Conjuring

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.590
films — and here's where things get interesting,
because there's not just one evil entity in

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.590
this movie.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.070
The demon we're calling the Ram was still
imprisoned inside the doll in the closet when

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:27.290
Janice had her first few brushes with the
supernatural, which means there must be another

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.930
demon in the Mullins' house.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:29.930
Which one?

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.650
We'll give you a hint: If it grabs you like
an evil nun, and dresses like an evil nun,

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.760
and pushes little wheelchair-bound children
into barns like an evil nun, it's probably

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:43.100
an evil freakin nun — also known as Valak,
the demonic entity whose sister act will headline

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.180
the next film in the franchise.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.780
It's not clear yet whether the Nun is specifically
connected to the Ram that possesses the Annabelle

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:53.400
doll, or whether she would've showed up to
help any evil spirit that had gotten itself

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.760
trapped in a closet.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.180
But with a creepy post-credits scene in Creation
that acts as a teaser for the Nun's stand-alone

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:04.210
film, we can be sure that in the tangled web
of the Conjuring universe, everything is connected.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:07.040
"Please, from the start."

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.150
Thanks for watching!

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.780
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:13.370
Plus, check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too.

